  "id": "COMPOUND:14339 - PROTEIN:5913",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the regulation of TAR DNA-binding protein 43 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that dexamethasone acts as a target for multiple compounds, including lapidilectine A, 14-(R)-9-Hydroxyl-2,3,10-Trimethoxytetrahyrdooxyprotoberberine, and Br-Xanthone A, all of which are known to target TAR DNA-binding protein 43. These compounds are likely acting through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating calmodulin, which serves as a central mediator in the signaling pathways that influence TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The presence of multiple pathways converging on calmodulin and ultimately on TAR DNA-binding protein 43 indicates a potential role for calmodulin in mediating the effects of these compounds. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that dexamethasone may influence TAR DNA-binding protein 43 through calmodulin, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the precise mechanism of action.",
